{"event_type": "agent.output", "trace_id": "dbe934c892c74558", "span_id": "261ae35e72fb42ae", "parent_span_id": "63a08288dc064970", "span_name": null, "sequence_id": 5, "timestamp_ns": 1784074241621546000, "payload": {"framework": "ms_agent_framework", "agent_name": "grid-load-forecaster", "chat_name": "grid-load-forecaster", "latency_ms": 2945.602, "output": {"message": {"ai_model_id": "gpt-4o-mini", "metadata": {"logprobs": null, "id": "chatcmpl-E1hUtT8RHV8pf0zj6zitaXnVzo0Xr", "created": 1784074239, "system_fingerprint": "fp_a23f63aa66", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 231, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}, "completion_tokens": 143, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}}}, "content_type": "message", "role": "assistant", "name": "grid-load-forecaster", "items": [{"ai_model_id": null, "metadata": {}, "content_type": "text", "text": "Forecasted evening peak demand is projected at 42.1 GW. With the current available capacity of 44.0 GW and an operating-reserve requirement of 3.0 GW, the reserve margin stands at 44.0 GW - 42.1 GW = 1.9 GW. This does not meet the required operating reserve, particularly with looming uncertainties in both wind generation and a derated combined-cycle unit that limits capacity. \n\nTo ensure reliable grid operation during the evening peak, I recommend issuing a demand-response call to reduce load quickly. This can help manage demand closer to available generation, ensuring reserves are sufficient to handle contingencies and safeguard grid reliability as evening temperatures rise during the heat advisory.", "encoding": null}], "encoding": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "status": null}, "thread": "<semantic_kernel.agents.chat_completion.chat_completion_agent.ChatHistoryAgentThread object at 0x12b3b6890>"}}, "hash": "sha256:354d23450ba3d75b8dc1858698df0f0751790d4d02b271f1e7047c2ebe3aaa16", "previous_hash": "sha256:c33